{
  "id": "c-open-altium-designer-cadence-orcad-openscad-task-01-windows",
  "snapshot": "OrCAD-Altium-openscad",
  "instruction": "Complete the task using command-line or batch-capable tools from Altium Designer, OrCAD Capture, or OpenSCAD. Two neutral schematic packages, `design_a` and `design_b`, are on the desktop. Extract every primitive part reference designator from both designs and write `merged_refdes.txt`. Requirements: - Prefix refdes from `design_a` with `A:` and refdes from `design_b` with `B:`. - Sort first by prefix (`A` before `B`), then lexicographically by the original refdes. - Use one refdes per line in `merged_refdes.txt`. [Software] Altium Designer is available at `D:\\Altium\\AD26\\X2.EXE`. OrCAD Capture is available at `D:\\orcad\\tools\\bin\\Capture.exe`. OpenSCAD is available as `openscad`.",
  "source": "https://www.altium.com/altium-designer; https://www.cadence.com/en_US/home/tools/pcb-design-and-analysis/orcad.html; https://openscad.org/; https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/OpenSCAD_User_Manual/Using_OpenSCAD_in_a_command_line_environment; https://www.ipc.org/ipc-2581",
